I’ve reduced the “closed form” request to a concrete indexed recurrence: one weighted variable is solved from exactly one coefficient \([X^{4t+1-j}]\) at each weight \(j\), using the already proved pivot \(p_C\), \(p_Q\), or \(p_{b_2}\). I’m implementing that recurrence directly in Singular so the controls do not depend on SymPy’s costly full expansion and so split fibers can be run componentwise.
