The coefficient-array recurrence is now fully explicit (binomial shift, Euler convolution, \(b_1\) removal, and the high-weight solves), and it gives the requested degree bounds uniformly. A useful simplification emerged: \(E_t\) is independent of the integration constant \(T(0)\), so that gauge can be omitted from terminal construction. I’m now specializing \(b_4\) before expansion; this is what makes the \(t=11\) product-factor control computationally realistic.
