+The only integer roots among the unindexed linear factors are `t=0` (the
+factor `t`) and `t=-1` (the factor `t+1`); the other displayed linear roots
+are nonintegral.  The indexed odd factor `4t-2j+1` cannot be zero and is
+positive in its stated ranges.  Equations (3.4)--(3.5) exclude all admissible
+roots of `F_C,F_Q`.  Thus the specialization-exception set for integer
