+```text
+sqrt(I_(t,+))=(b3,u_2,...,u_(t-1))  for t=3,4,5,6.   (6.1)
+```
+
+The `t=5,6` instances are new exact promotions.  They remain fixed-integer
+proofs, not an induction.  On both `t=6` fibres modulo `1009`, the weaker
+uniform-looking augmented chain also holds: after adjoining successively
+`b3,u5,...,u_(j+1)`, the reduction of `u_j^7` is zero.  This is
+**MEASURED-MODULAR** evidence for exponent `t+1`; no symbolic leading
+coefficient has been obtained.
+
+There is a useful correction at `t=2`.  The positive rows are not literally
+all zero in `A_2`: the stored band-three row at `b4=0` is
