+## 7. Assembly and exact theorem status
+
+Let `I_t=<T_(t,0),...,T_(t,2t-1)>`.  If the `b4=0` chart is unit, then `b4`
+is invertible in the quotient by `I_t`.  If the dehomogenized `b4=1` chart is
+unit, weighted homogeneity clears a power of `b4` and shows that `b4` is
+nilpotent in the same quotient.  An element cannot be both invertible and
+nilpotent in a nonzero ring, so `I_t=[1]`.  Equivalently this is the standard
+two-chart cover, with no saturation component suppressed.
